# Herald Core

- Module: `github.com/SolaTyolo/herald`. Project name: **Herald**.
- Channel providers: Traefik-style YAML routing; builtin only `smtp_email` / `inapp`; other channels are user-implemented remote HTTP workers (`POST /delivery`). Do not add in-process plugin runtimes.
- `cmd/api` and `cmd/worker` must NOT import user provider implementations.
- Delivery: `routing.Table.ProvidersForChannel` + builtin SMTP (`SMTP_*` env) / inapp; remote → `POST /delivery` + Redis result queue (default) or sync HTTP body. Remote secrets stay in the worker.
- Auth: required env `API_KEY`; `Authorization: Bearer` constant-time compare. No Tenant/Environment/`env_id` — single global data namespace.
- Persistence: `repository.Store` via `repository.Open()` — business layers use the Store port only.
- Missing records: use `repository.IsNotFound(err)`.
- `QUEUE_MODE=local` runs jobs in-process and does not use Redis. `QUEUE_MODE=asynq` splits `RoleAPI` (migrations, bridge subscriber) and `RoleWorker` (Asynq); both share `PROVIDERS_CONFIG` and `REDIS_ADDR`.
- User Delivery Workers are external processes. Core posts `pkg/contract.DeliveryRequest` and must not import user provider implementations.
- Minimize diff scope; match existing patterns.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
